      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5cc03aac564a7e69a599e019|full_name}: Thanks for your reply! I understand SLI won't make VRC run at smooth 90fps, it won't fix anything yes, but at least we will gain more fps, which, some people are willing to pay for.\n\nActually in SteamVR, we can see whether fps is bounded by CPU or GPU. Yes, VRC is sometime bounded by CPU but is also sometime bounded by GPU. SLI may increase fps when it is bounded by GPU.\nhttps://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/SteamVR/Frame_Timing \n\nBy the way, it depends on your HMD but seems like you are more likely bounded by your CPU rather than GPU",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
